 Masters degree in computer science, acoustics, signal processing, electronics, or a related field;
 Programming skills in Python. Familiarity with ML frameworks (PyTorch, Tensorfiow, Jax) is a bonus;
 Skills/experience in working with low-resource IT platforms and embedded development (e.g. tinyML, hardware hacking, zig, demo scene) are a bonus;
 Demonstrated interest in biodiversity, animal behaviour, or animal sound;
 Proficient in spoken and written English;
 A team player who can communicate well also across scientific fields and teams;
 Highly motivated and organised self-starter with an open mindset.
 What we offer 
